package pages

import "github.com/tuxedocurly/wledger/internal/auth"
import "github.com/tuxedocurly/wledger/web/layouts"

templ LEDTestCentre(user auth.User) {
	@layouts.Base("LED Test Centre", user) {
		<script src="/static/js/led_test_centre.js"></script>
		<div x-data="ledTestCentre()" x-cloak class="space-y-4">
			<div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-2"><h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">LED Test Centre</h1><div class="flex gap-2"><a href="/hardware" class="btn btn-sm">Hardware</a><a href="/settings" class="btn btn-sm">Function settings</a></div></div>
			<p>Loading this page reads saved data only. Test Connection explicitly inspects a controller without changing its output. Physical tests require an explicit command. Server-managed flash and sequence stop after the requested duration.</p>
			<p class="alert alert-warning" x-show="!data.physical_output_enabled">Physical output is disabled. Mapping changes remain explicit database actions.</p>
			<p role="alert" class="text-error" x-text="error"></p><p role="status" x-text="notice"></p>
			<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
				<label>Controller<select aria-label="Controller" class="select select-bordered" x-model="controllerID" @change="controllerChanged()" :disabled="busy"><option value="">Choose controller</option><template x-for="c in data.controllers" :key="c.id"><option :value="c.id" x-text="c.name + ' · ' + c.led_count + ' pixels · ' + (c.verified ? 'configured verified' : 'not verified')"></option></template></select></label>
				<label>Output<select aria-label="Output" class="select select-bordered" x-model="outputOrder" @change="outputChanged()" :disabled="busy"><option value="">Whole controller</option><template x-for="o in outputs" :key="o.order"><option :value="o.order" x-text="'Output ' + o.order + ' · ' + o.start + '–' + (o.start + o.length - 1)"></option></template></select></label>
				<button class="btn" @click="inspect()" :disabled="busy || !controllerID">Test Connection (read-only)</button><a class="btn btn-secondary" :href="controllerID ? '/hardware/' + controllerID + '/wiring-designer' : '/hardware'" :aria-disabled="!controllerID">Open Graphical Wiring Designer</a><button class="btn btn-outline" @click="refresh()" :disabled="busy">Refresh saved data</button>
			</div>
			<div x-show="inspection"><p x-text="'Capacity: ' + inspection?.capacity + ' · Firmware: ' + inspection?.firmware"></p><template x-for="o in outputs" :key="o.order"><p x-text="'Output ' + o.order + ': start ' + o.start + ', length ' + o.length + ', first/last ' + o.first_index + '/' + o.last_index + ', pins ' + JSON.stringify(o.pins) + ', reversed ' + o.reversed"></p></template></div>
			<nav class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-label="Test centre sections"><template x-for="name in tabs" :key="name"><button class="btn btn-sm" :class="tab === name ? 'btn-primary' : 'btn-outline'" :aria-pressed="tab === name" @click="tab = name" x-text="name"></button></template></nav>
			<div class="card bg-base-200"><div class="card-body gap-3">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><label>Absolute pixel (0-based)<input type="number" class="input input-bordered" x-model.number="pixel" :min="limits.start" :max="limits.start + limits.count - 1"/></label><label>Count<input type="number" min="1" class="input input-bordered" x-model.number="count"/></label><label>Colour<input type="color" x-model="color"/></label><label>Brightness (0–255)<input class="input input-bordered" type="number" min="0" max="255" x-model.number="brightness"/></label><label>Duration seconds<input class="input input-bordered" type="number" min="1" max="3600" x-model.number="duration"/></label><label>Mode<select class="select select-bordered" x-model="mode"><option>solid</option><option>flash</option><option>sequence</option></select></label></div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><span>Use saved function style:</span><template x-for="name in Object.keys(data.styles || {})" :key="name"><button class="btn btn-xs" @click="applyStyle(name)" x-text="name"></button></template><span>Local test overrides only; edit defaults in Settings.</span></div>
								<p x-text="'Controller absolute: ' + pixel + ' · Output relative (0-based): ' + (pixel - limits.start) + ' · Selected bounds: ' + limits.start + '–' + (limits.start + limits.count - 1)"></p>
				<p>Pixel window: at most 96 pixels; click selects only, never sends a command. Drawer range numbering below is cabinet-based (1-based), not controller absolute.</p>
				<p class="flex flex-wrap gap-3" aria-label="Pixel assignment legend"><span class="text-success">● Assigned</span><span>○ Unassigned</span><span class="text-error">! Conflict / invalid mapping</span><span>Outline marks selection. Colours describe saved mappings, not physical verification.</span></p>
								<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1" aria-label="Controller pixel map"><template x-for="p in pixelWindow" :key="p.pixel"><button class="btn btn-xs" :class="[p.status === 'conflict' ? 'btn-error' : p.status === 'assigned' ? 'btn-success' : '', p.pixel === Number(pixel) ? 'btn-outline' : '']" :aria-label="'Pixel ' + p.pixel + ': ' + p.status" :aria-pressed="p.pixel === Number(pixel)" @click="pixel = p.pixel" x-text="p.pixel"></button></template></div>
								<section aria-label="Selected pixel assignments" class="border rounded p-3 space-y-2"><h2 class="font-bold" x-text="'Pixel ' + pixel + ': ' + selectedPixel.status"></h2><p x-show="!selectedPixel.assignments.length">No drawer range assignment returned for this controller pixel.</p><template x-for="(a, i) in selectedPixel.assignments" :key="i"><div><a class="link" :href="'/storage/cabinets/' + a.cabinet.id" x-text="'Cabinet: ' + a.cabinet.name + ' (#' + a.cabinet.id + ')'"></a><span> · </span><a class="link" :href="'/storage/drawers/' + a.drawer.id" x-text="'Drawer: ' + a.drawer.label + ' (#' + a.drawer.id + ')'"></a><p x-text="'Drawer-relative pixel (0-based): ' + a.relative"></p><p x-show="!a.bins.length">No explicitly mapped bin at this pixel; drawer assignment only.</p></div></template><template x-for="(b, i) in selectedPixel.bins" :key="i"><p x-text="'Bin: ' + b.label + ' (#' + b.id + ') · Drawer ' + b.drawer.label + ' · Cabinet ' + b.cabinet.name + ' · relative pixel (0-based): ' + (b.relative_pixel ?? 'unresolved') + (b.stale ? ' · STALE' : '')"></p></template><p class="text-error" x-show="selectedPixel.status === 'conflict'">Conflicting, stale, or invalid saved mapping. Review all assignments and validation before testing or changing it.</p><template x-for="(v, i) in selectedPixel.findings" :key="i"><p class="text-error" x-text="v.message + ' Repair: ' + v.repair"></p></template></section>
				<div class="flex gap-2"><button class="btn btn-sm" @click="move(-1)">Previous pixel (select)</button><button class="btn btn-sm" @click="move(1)">Next pixel (select)</button></div>
				<fieldset :disabled="busy || !controllerID || !data.physical_output_enabled" class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" x-show="['controller','pixel','discovery'].includes(tab)">
					<button class="btn btn-primary" @click="testPixel()">Test / replay individual pixel</button><button class="btn" @click="testPixel()">Identify selected pixel</button><button class="btn" @click="testPixel(0, 'solid', '#000000')">Individual pixel OFF</button><button class="btn" @click="testPixel(0, 'flash')">Flash individual pixel</button><button class="btn" @click="testPixel(-1)">Previous pixel and test</button><button class="btn" @click="testPixel(1)">Next pixel and test</button><button class="btn" @click="start('test_pixel')">Test explicit range</button><button class="btn" @click="start('test_pixel', true)">All selected output on</button><button class="btn" @click="start('test_pixel', true, '#000000')">Selected output off</button>
					<button class="btn" @click="start('test_pixel', false, '#ff0000')">Red range</button><button class="btn" @click="start('test_pixel', false, '#00ff00')">Green range</button><button class="btn" @click="start('test_pixel', false, '#0000ff')">Blue range</button>
					<button class="btn" @click="mode = 'flash'; start('test_pixel')">Flash range</button><button class="btn" @click="mode = 'sequence'; start('test_pixel', true)">Sequential output test</button>
				</fieldset>
			</div></div>
			<fieldset :disabled="busy" x-show="['drawer','discovery','allocation'].includes(tab)" class="space-y-3">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><label>Cabinet<select aria-label="Cabinet" class="select select-bordered" x-model="cabinetID" @change="drawerID = ''; allocationIDs = []; invalidate()" :disabled="busy"><option value="">Choose cabinet</option><template x-for="c in data.cabinets" :key="c.id"><option :value="c.id" x-text="c.name"></option></template></select></label><label>Drawer<select aria-label="Drawer" class="select select-bordered" x-model="drawerID" @change="invalidate()" :disabled="busy"><option value="">Choose drawer</option><template x-for="d in drawers" :key="d.id"><option :value="d.id" x-text="d.label"></option></template></select></label><label>Bin<select aria-label="Bin" class="select select-bordered" x-model="binID" :disabled="busy"><option value="">No bin</option><template x-for="b in (drawer?.bins || [])" :key="b.id"><option :value="b.id" x-text="b.label"></option></template></select></label></div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><button class="btn" @click="start('locate_cabinet')" :disabled="busy || !cabinetID || !data.physical_output_enabled">Test cabinet allocated pixels</button><a class="link" :href="cabinetID ? '/storage/cabinets/' + cabinetID + '/edit' : '/storage/cabinets'">Edit cabinet and drawer layout</a></div>
									<p>Existing drawer ranges (cabinet numbering; logical allocations, not physical order):</p>
									<p x-text="'Drawer allocated count: ' + (drawer?.ranges || []).reduce((total, range) => total + Number(range.count), 0)"></p>
								<template x-for="(r, i) in (drawer?.ranges || [])" :key="i"><p class="border-l-4 border-primary pl-2" x-text="'Cabinet range ' + r.start + '–' + (Number(r.start) + Number(r.count) - 1) + ' (' + r.count + ' pixels)'"></p></template>
				<p x-show="tab === 'drawer'">Drawer tests use all controllers resolved from its saved mapping, independent of the controller/output selection above. A selected bin is used only by Test selected mapped bin.</p>
								<fieldset x-show="tab === 'drawer'" :disabled="busy || !drawerID || !data.physical_output_enabled" class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><template x-for="f in ['locate_drawer','drawer_first','drawer_last','drawer_bins','drawer_sequence','drawer_flash','drawer_all']" :key="f"><button class="btn" @click="start(f)" x-text="f.replaceAll('_',' ')"></button></template><button class="btn" @click="start('drawer_bin')" :disabled="!binID">Test selected mapped bin</button></fieldset>
				<div x-show="tab === 'discovery'" class="space-y-2"><p>Test pixels above, then mark the endpoints. The backend converts absolute controller indices to cabinet numbering; the frontend never assumes a cabinet offset. Reversed endpoint order is rejected.</p><button class="btn" @click="mark('first')">Mark selected as first</button><button class="btn" @click="mark('last')">Mark selected as last</button><p x-text="'Marked first: ' + first + ' · last: ' + last"></p><button class="btn" @click="mappingPreview(true)" :disabled="busy">Preview drawer mapping</button><button class="btn btn-outline" @click="saveBin()" :disabled="busy || !binID">Save selected pixel to bin…</button><button class="btn btn-outline" @click="clearBin()" :disabled="busy || !binID">Clear selected bin pixel override…</button></div>
				<div x-show="tab === 'allocation'" class="space-y-2"><p>Select drawers in allocation order. Changing inputs requires a new preview.</p><template x-for="d in drawers" :key="d.id"><label class="inline-flex gap-2 mr-4"><input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" :value="String(d.id)" x-model="allocationIDs" @change="preview = []; mappingConfirmed = false"/><span x-text="d.label"></span></label></template><p x-text="'Allocation order (drawer IDs): ' + allocationIDs.join(', ')"></p><label>Cabinet start (1-based)<input type="number" min="1" class="input input-bordered" x-model.number="cabinetStart" @input="preview = []; mappingConfirmed = false"/></label><label>Pixels per drawer<input type="number" min="1" class="input input-bordered" x-model.number="perDrawer" @input="preview = []; mappingConfirmed = false"/></label><button class="btn" @click="mappingPreview(false)" :disabled="busy">Preview allocation</button></div>
				<div x-show="preview.length" class="card bg-base-200"><div class="card-body"><h2 class="card-title">Append-only proposals</h2><p class="text-warning">Existing multiple-range mappings must remain intact. Saving appends ranges, never replaces them. Edited proposals are revalidated atomically by the backend, including overlaps and ownership.</p><template x-for="(row, i) in preview" :key="i"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><span x-text="'Drawer ' + row.drawer_id"></span><label>Cabinet start<input type="number" min="1" class="input input-bordered" x-model.number="row.start" @input="mappingConfirmed = false"/></label><label>Count<input type="number" min="1" class="input input-bordered" x-model.number="row.count" @input="mappingConfirmed = false"/></label></div></template><p role="alert" x-show="conflicts.length" x-text="JSON.stringify(conflicts)"></p><label><input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" x-model="mappingConfirmed"/> I reviewed these cabinet coordinates and confirm appending these ranges.</label><button class="btn btn-primary" @click="saveMapping()" :disabled="busy || !mappingConfirmed || conflicts.length > 0">Save mapping append</button></div></div>
			</fieldset>
			<section x-show="tab === 'validation'"><h2 class="text-lg font-bold">Saved-data validation (no hardware contact)</h2><p x-show="!data.validation?.length">No validation findings returned.</p><template x-for="(v, i) in (data.validation || [])" :key="i"><div class="card bg-base-200 mb-2"><div class="card-body"><p x-text="v.severity + ': ' + v.message"></p><p x-text="'Controller ' + v.controller_id + ' · cabinet ' + v.cabinet_id + ' · drawer ' + v.drawer_id + ' · bin ' + v.bin_id"></p><p x-text="'Repair: ' + v.repair"></p></div></div></template></section>
			<section class="card border border-warning"><div class="card-body"><h2 class="card-title">Command evidence &amp; stop controls</h2><p x-text="sent"></p><p x-text="acknowledged"></p><label><input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" x-model="human"/> I observed the intended physical behaviour (local note only; never application verification).</label><label>Chosen operation<select class="select select-bordered" x-model="chosen"><option value="">Select operation</option><template x-for="op in operations" :key="op.id"><option :value="op.id" x-text="op.id + ' · ' + op.state"></option></template></select></label><button class="btn btn-warning" @click="stop(chosen)" :disabled="busy || !chosen">Stop chosen operation</button><template x-for="op in operations" :key="op.id"><div class="border rounded p-2"><p x-text="'Operation ' + op.id + ' · Controller ' + op.controller + ' · State ' + op.state"></p><p x-text="'Last command: ' + op.last + ' · Last successful command: ' + op.successful"></p><p class="text-error" x-text="op.error"></p><button class="btn btn-sm" @click="stop(op.id)" :disabled="busy">Stop / retry Stop</button></div></template><p>No automatic browser cycling or polling. Refresh saved data to see server-managed operation progress. Acknowledgement does not prove LEDs lit or switched off. Stop clears only owned ranges; it does not recreate an unknown pre-test framebuffer or external animation. Put test ranges into a known off/solid baseline before commissioning.</p></div></section>
			<button class="btn btn-error" @click="emergencyOpen = true; emergencyText = ''">Emergency global off…</button>
			<div x-show="emergencyOpen" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Confirm emergency global off" class="card border border-error bg-base-200"><div class="card-body"><h2 class="card-title">Emergency global off</h2><p>This explicitly sends OFF to all backend-targeted controllers, not only the selection. Type EMERGENCY OFF to confirm.</p><label>Confirmation<input class="input input-bordered" x-model="emergencyText" autocomplete="off"/></label><button class="btn btn-error" @click="emergency()" :disabled="busy || emergencyText !== 'EMERGENCY OFF'">Send global emergency off</button><button class="btn" @click="emergencyOpen = false" :disabled="busy">Cancel</button></div></div>
			<section x-show="emergencyResults.length" aria-label="Emergency off outcomes"><h2 class="font-bold">Persisted emergency off outcomes</h2><p>Unresolved outcomes block new operations until safely reconciled and Emergency Off is retried.</p><template x-for="(r, i) in emergencyResults" :key="i"><p :class="r.Acknowledged ? 'text-success' : 'text-error'" x-text="'Controller ' + r.ControllerID + ' · ' + (r.Address || '') + ':' + (r.Port || '') + ': ' + (r.Acknowledged ? 'acknowledged (not physically verified)' : r.Attempted ? 'attempted, not acknowledged' : 'unattempted') + ' ' + (r.Error || '')"></p></template></section>
		</div>
	}
}
